# Information Disclosure - Hardcoded Database Credentials Exposed via Backup Source Code

## Executive Summary

An information disclosure vulnerability was identified due to the exposure of a backup source code file within a publicly accessible directory.

The application's `robots.txt` file disclosed the existence of a `/backup` directory containing a Java backup file (`ProductTemplate.java.bak`). The exposed source code contained hardcoded PostgreSQL database credentials, including the database password.

Disclosure of source code and embedded credentials provides attackers with valuable reconnaissance information and may enable unauthorized access to backend systems if the exposed credentials are valid.

