# Vulnerability Details

The application unintentionally exposes backup source code files through a publicly accessible web directory.

The retrieved Java source code contains the database connection configuration embedded directly within the application logic.

The following connection parameters are disclosed:

```java
ConnectionBuilder.from(
    "org.postgresql.Driver",
    "postgresql",
    "localhost",
    5432,
    "postgres",
    "postgres",
    "e05aa1uyi9ekrr0qnxxi4jk2xf6deucb"
)
```

Among these values, the final argument corresponds to the PostgreSQL database password.

Embedding credentials directly in source code significantly increases the impact of any source code disclosure vulnerability.

