# Key Takeaways

* Backup files should never be publicly accessible.
* Source code exposure often reveals significantly more than application logic.
* Hardcoded credentials dramatically increase the impact of source code disclosure.
* Secrets should be stored outside application code using dedicated secret management mechanisms.
* Regular security reviews should verify that development artifacts and backup files are excluded from production deployments.
